# The Device label, branch by branch - minimal-cuda-ofx, Windows 11 + RTX 3060, 2026-11-28
#
# The contract suite can only render the CPU branch: FakeHost::render() sets
# kOfxImageEffectPropCudaEnabled=0 at all three call sites, so the plug-in's own
# PathLabel() is exercised with the host-pointer facts and the label reads
# "CPU_ONLY - ...". The CUDA_ONLY wording is reached in processImagesCuda(), which
# needs a host that hands device pointers - no host on this machine does (Resolve's
# script server refuses, Natron is not installed, the fake host does not hand CUDA).
#
# So the label moved into src/ExecutionMode.h, where the plug-in and the mode test call
# one PathLabel(), and the mode test now asserts the CUDA_ONLY side and prints every
# label it sees. What that proves: the string, for both branches, through the function
# the plug-in uses. What it does not prove: the property write on a CUDA render - that
# still needs a host or a fake host that hands a device pointer, and it is named as
# unproven in references/cuda-streams-and-memory.md section 4.
#
# Command: templates/minimal-cuda-ofx/test/run-tests.bat Release (which builds the
# plug-in, runs the contract suite three times plus the gpux pass, then the mode test).

